diskformer.js — engines/

The WGSL kernels in these engines are ports of browser-big-fast-lab's custom-kernels engine, an Apache-2.0
fork of gemma4-webgpu:

  gemma4-webgpu
  Copyright 2026 Tyler Straub
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (engines/LICENSE-APACHE)
  https://github.com/tylerstraub/gemma4-webgpu

Changes from the original: rewritten for mixture-of-experts models whose experts stream from OPFS (Q8_0 and Q4_0
split planes, slot-indexed expert GEMVs, GPU router top-k, chunked prefill, Q6_K head planes). `ternary_bonsai_2_dflash.js` is built from NakliTechie/dflash-mlx-bonsai2 (Apache-2.0). `lfm2_5.js`,
`gemma-4-e2b.js` and `ternary_bonsai_2_27b.js` are built from webml-community Hugging Face Spaces by the same author, MIT.
`clover_moe_ssd.js` follows the math of Diffuspace's modeling_clover_moe.py (Apache-2.0, Clover-35B-A3B-Preview); no
code is copied. `vendor/kohra-denoise.js` is kohra.js's denoise.js, unchanged (NakliTechie/kohra.js, Apache-2.0,
engines/LICENSE-APACHE), checked by scripts/sync-kohra.mjs. Everything else in
this folder is MIT (../LICENSE), Copyright (c) 2026 Chirag Patnaik.

The engine files are copies of LocalMind's (https://github.com/NakliTechie/LocalMind), kept in step by
scripts/sync-localmind.mjs. Model weights are not distributed: each model is downloaded by the user under its own
terms (Gemma: https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms; Qwen3.6: Apache-2.0; each other model under its own license).
